Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:26:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(db): S1 R4 TRUNCATE controls expect the verifier's
 quoted-identifier diagnostic (S1-R4-A-01)

verify.sql emits API-role privilege problems through format('%I: %s still holds %s'),
so the mixed-case relation arrives double-quoted: `"MuxProcessedEvent": anon still
holds TRUNCATE` (observed verbatim in the B1 composed verifier output). The first R4
draft of the shared controls searched for the unquoted spelling and could never match.

- s1-truncate-controls.sh: exact fixed-string needles in S1_TRUNC_MSG_* and
  s1_trunc_msg_count (grep -F); C1/C2 additionally assert the other role is NOT named;
  predecessor checks are labelled psql-route only (the predecessor is not run through
  Prisma; the Prisma route is asserted for the current verifier).
- s1-r4-truncate-discriminator.sh: precondition decision is taken BEFORE the optional
  synthetic marker INSERT, so a failed precondition issues no INSERT/GRANT/REVOKE; the
  message says exactly that instead of "nothing mutated".
- new test/db/s1-r4-truncate-message-spec.sh: offline (bash+grep, no database) spec
  that pins the needles to verify.sql's format strings and to real B1 fragments, and
  rejects wrong role, wrong privilege, wrong class, the OK notice and the unquoted
  spelling.

verify.sql, migration.sql, down.sql, the target guard, the bootstrap and the full
harness are byte-identical to 41f4d6a9. No database run has happened.
